.TH FMT_ESCAPECHARQUOTEDSHELL 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
fmt_escapecharquotedshell \- Escape characters for quoted shell format

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/fmt.h>

.IB size_t
.IB fmt_escapecharquotedshell(char* dest, int chr);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBfmt_escapecharquotedshell\fR function escapes characters for quoted shell format. It takes a destination buffer and a character as arguments. The function escapes the character if it is a single quote (`'`), otherwise it copies the character unchanged.

The function takes the following parameters:
.IB char*
A pointer to the destination buffer.
.IB int
The character to escape.

The function returns the number of bytes written to the destination buffer.

The \fBfmt_escapecharquotedshell\fR function is intended to be used to escape characters for quoted shell format, such as to safely include shell commands within quotes.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBfmt_escapecharquotedshell\fR function to escape characters for quoted shell format:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/fmt.h>

int main() {
    char dest[20];
    int c = '\'';

    size_t written = fmt_escapecharquotedshell(dest, c);

    printf("Written %d bytes: %s\n", written, dest);

    return 0;
}
.nef